  "full_text": "Okay, so in Monkville, it's time for evening prayer. Although I'm going to be up, I stay up like 48 hours. But anyway, just for the fuck of it. Or not 40. Anyway, evening prayer. So like, Mr. God. So prayer is supposed to entertain God. That's the purpose of prayer. Mr. God. What do you think of burping? I don't know why I thought of that. What do you think, Mr. God? It's very rude, isn't it? Mr. God says. It's very, very rude. What about if you're alone? Should you burp when you're alone, or does that offend the angels? Mr. God says. Okay, Mr. God says. Priest shall take some of the blood on his finger, sprinkle it seven times toward the front of the meeting tent. Then the heifer shall be burned in his sight, with its hide and flesh and its blood and offal. And the priest shall take some cedar wood. hyssop and scarlet yarn and throw them into the fire in the midst which the heifer is being burned the priest shall then wash his garments and bathe his body in water he remains unclean until the evening and only after may he return to the camp likewise he who burned the heifer shall wash his garments bathe his body in water and be cleansed until evening so like i send diana I took a shower, like, second time today. Because you stink when you stay up for two days. So, like, it's important. Because, like, God gets very angry if you stink. Because, like, he can't stand the smell or some shit. I don't know. I'm not sure why. He doesn't like you smelling stink. Because it freaks him out. The guy's like totally freaked out. Like, oh my God. I don't know.",
